# The throw: its key plays the arm's throw (Throwing: its pack reads it); the clip's marker,
# frag.release, lets go of the one carried, with 2.5 s to live.
#
# The grenade going off: when its time is up, every simulation sets it off where it is, on the same
# tick (so the blast is never a lead late). The numbers are the frag mod's (its options, published
# as fields); hurting who is near is the mod's too (combat.damage).

motion Throwing on use
	cooldown 0.7
	lasts 0.7

motion Release on frag.release
	item carried
	emit frag.thrown
	launch carried speed 15 lift 3 ahead 0.8 seconds 2.5

motion Blast on expired
	owner item
	emit frag.blast
	break radius frag.break_radius speed frag.push seconds frag.rubble_seconds
	find Blast bodies
		impulse (distance < frag.radius) * frag.push * (1 - distance / frag.radius) along away
		impulse (distance < frag.radius) * 0.35 * frag.push * (1 - distance / frag.radius) along up
